@startuml Scenario_4_Multi_Organization

title Scenario 4: Multi-Organization Collaboration\nMnDOT + External Engineering Consultant

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam participant {
    FontSize 11
}

box "MnDOT Enterprise" #E8F5E9
    actor "Facility\nAsset Mgmt" as FAC
    database "MnDOT\nCIR" as CIR
end box

participant "ISBM\nProvider" as ISBM

box "ACME Engineering (Consultant)" #E3F2FD
    actor "Project\nDesign Team" as ACME
end box

note over ISBM
  **MnDOT Facility channels**
  /mndot/{facility-fed-id}/engineering/publication
  /mndot/{facility-fed-id}/engineering/request

  **Consultant Project channels**
  /acme-eng/{project-fed-id}/engineering/publication

  **Enterprise CIR**
  /mndot/enterprise/cir/request
end note

== Security: Token-Based Access Control ==

note over FAC, ISBM
  MnDOT grants ACME a **read-only token**
  for the facility engineering channels.
  ACME authenticates with:
  Authorization: Basic <token>
end note

note over ISBM, ACME
  ACME grants MnDOT a **read-only token**
  for the project engineering channel.
end note

== Data Flow: Consultant Reads → Designs → Delivers ==

ACME -> ISBM: OpenConsumerRequestSession\n  /mndot/{facility-fed-id}/engineering/request\n  Authorization: Basic <mndot-token>
ISBM --> ACME: sessionId (authorized)

ACME -> ISBM: PostRequest: "Current state of Bridge 9340"
FAC -> ISBM: ReadRequest → PostResponse (as-built data)
ACME -> ISBM: ReadResponse → receives current state

|||
note over ACME: Design work happens\n(weeks/months)
|||

ACME -> ISBM: PostPublication\n  /acme-eng/{project-fed-id}/engineering/publication\n  Approved design changes

ISBM -> FAC: PUT /notifications/...\n  (MnDOT subscribed to consultant's channel)

FAC -> ISBM: ReadPublication → approved changes
FAC -> CIR: Register identity mappings\n  (consultant IDs ↔ facility IDs)
CIR --> FAC: AcknowledgeRegistry

== Contract Ends ==

note over FAC, ACME
  **MnDOT revokes ACME's token**
  ✗ ACME can no longer open sessions on MnDOT channels
  ✓ Consultant's project channels remain (owned by ACME)
  ✓ CIR identity mappings retained permanently
  ✓ MnDOT revokes its own token on ACME's channels
end note

@enduml
